     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">It sounds like you&#39;re looking for open population models, which are implemented in unmarked with the <a rel=\"nofollow\">pcountopen function</a>. <div>Some papers to get you started: </div><div>- <a href=\"https://sci-hub.tw/https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1541-0420.2010.01465.x\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sci-hub.tw/https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1541-0420.2010.01465.x&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tv2uBg-pteXDhapSkcGZC\">Dail &amp; Madsen 2011</a></div><div>- <a href=\"https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1890/14-1487.1?casa_token=nmFbNqRiO98AAAAA:O3Z2v4P2lGHPOdZY7JASwJ7E5Go4vpc_yTJr2LHIlnX2ru5YKJ88azWfSJqxVE6Qd2UxIwt1SLp3w84\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1890/14-1487.1?casa_token%3DnmFbNqRiO98AAAAA:O3Z2v4P2lGHPOdZY7JASwJ7E5Go4vpc_yTJr2LHIlnX2ru5YKJ88azWfSJqxVE6Qd2UxIwt1SLp3w84&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1gZHF-edJyXocuVCADDwNo\">Hostetler and Chandler 2015</a></div><div>- <a href=\"https://sci-hub.tw/https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12572\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sci-hub.tw/https://doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12572&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0_Tq-_u7jEo1HE1wehARbl\">Bellier, Kéry, and Schaub 2016</a></div><div>- <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10144-017-0600-7.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10144-017-0600-7.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wBoq9iQ71C1hl5-4x2Gb_\">Zhao, Royle, and Boomer 2017</a></div><div>- and a reminder that these models can be pretty sensitive to model assumptions: <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304380018300607/pdfft?casa_token=d8foSARhaLwAAAAA:lEGlCqaHYuwrfeMWDQ-C9sfbRfhU7J3TC3UpxY4lIFE5VFaUi6F0eQOCWCVQir0GVtxNLB2jRQ&amp;md5=01f6f53db8c905a4653bc5a5797f9b08&amp;pid=1-s2.0-S0304380018300607-main.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304380018300607/pdfft?casa_token%3Dd8foSARhaLwAAAAA:lEGlCqaHYuwrfeMWDQ-C9sfbRfhU7J3TC3UpxY4lIFE5VFaUi6F0eQOCWCVQir0GVtxNLB2jRQ%26md5%3D01f6f53db8c905a4653bc5a5797f9b08%26pid%3D1-s2.0-S0304380018300607-main.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0LD6AW5yOWodjDPU6e2Eoj\">Duarte, Adams, and Peterson 2018</a> , <a href=\"https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/ecs2.2791\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/ecs2.2791&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0GtWku9NkdYiYUs-HHHCkt\">Monroe et al. 2019</a> or <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304380018304186/pdfft?casa_token=7MncqkF94_MAAAAA:GgCrHgEVbuH0SZ3rYnMp1N63PtX0pVlsJhhye_QoCAUJ6KtpoW5nxjo1APkhFUKvOr6ry-ed4g&amp;md5=a2d5c398759ef4050b9c049c75e98335&amp;pid=1-s2.0-S0304380018304186-main.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304380018304186/pdfft?casa_token%3D7MncqkF94_MAAAAA:GgCrHgEVbuH0SZ3rYnMp1N63PtX0pVlsJhhye_QoCAUJ6KtpoW5nxjo1APkhFUKvOr6ry-ed4g%26md5%3Da2d5c398759ef4050b9c049c75e98335%26pid%3D1-s2.0-S0304380018304186-main.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792450523279000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FRW9boG1itKFqJG8RU6zm\">Zhao and Royle 2019</a></div><div>- 